 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\,i+(t+1)^{2}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{cot}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $(t+1)^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414" :knowledge-point/title "Domains of Functions With Trigonometric Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58429169-2633-55be-85e7-83421813d1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383490} {:answer/id #uuid "d036277f-1435-53a2-80ee-4bd475c464ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383491} {:answer/id #uuid "dd586afe-a6de-5462-a930-3e7e55dbbaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383492} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0b5f7a-b6da-52d7-bfa3-31cd6bf05a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383493} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee43416-5a14-5ef3-ad60-4107e624d588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee43416-5a14-5ef3-ad60-4107e624d588" :ans